WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You both are
New York City guys.

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:02.602 align:start size:94% position:6%
But very different parts of
New York City.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:06.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Very, very.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.039 --> 00:00:10.677
Colin is from Staten Island,
and I'm from the projects.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:11.211 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:11.211 --> 00:00:13.947 align:start size:94% position:6%
So it's two different corners
of the world.

00:00:13.947 --> 00:00:16.516
-There were more whoos for the
projects than for Staten Island,

00:00:16.516 --> 00:00:17.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
I just want to point out.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:20.120 size:88% position:44%
-We, obviously, we share
a history "SNL" now of

00:00:20.120 --> 00:00:21.354 line:92%
being "Weekend Update" anchors.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.690 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys -- now we share
something else.

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:24.424 size:81% position:41% line:92%
You guys were promoted

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:26.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
to co-head writers
earlier this year.

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:27.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
Congratulations.
-Yeah.

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:30.497 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:33.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How -- How have you found it
so far?

00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:34.401 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-I mean, as you know,

00:00:34.401 --> 00:00:37.270
you're basically doing the job
already before you get the job.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:40.840
-Right. They don't give it
to you unless you can do it.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:41.408 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Right, yeah.

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:44.077
-They're not like, "Here's some
scripts. Just see what happens."

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:46.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's basically the same job
you were already doing,

00:00:46.646 --> 00:00:49.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you have maybe
like 10 times the stress.

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:49.916 size:84% position:42% line:92%
Like, way more anxiety,

00:00:49.916 --> 00:00:52.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
but you can't do any more work
than you're already doing.

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:53.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like planning
someone else's wedding.

00:00:56.756 --> 00:00:57.690 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Constantly planning.

00:00:57.690 --> 00:01:00.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you mess it up,
they're very mad at you.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:03.663
-You're planning Lorne's wedding
every week.

00:01:03.663 --> 00:01:05.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I texted you
congratulations,

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:05.999 line:92%
and then you didn't write back,

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:07.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I saw you at a party
and I said,

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:08.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, is your phone number
the same?"

00:01:08.735 --> 00:01:09.602 line:92%
You're, like, "I just didn't --

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:11.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't even know how to feel
about it yet."

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:12.739 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.507 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's a tough situation
now

00:01:14.507 --> 00:01:15.341 line:92%
because I got a lot of friends

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:18.311
that work in comedy and they're
always, like, "Hey, man.

00:01:18.311 --> 00:01:19.145 line:92%
Could you help me get on 'SNL'"?

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.815
And I'm always like, "Yeah, I
don't got no power there."

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:23.950 size:88% position:44%
And now I'm head writer,
I got to like tell them,

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:26.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Hey, it's because I don't
believe in you.

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:28.521 line:92%
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:32.959 size:84% position:42%
"I'm not going help you
for that reason only."

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:35.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
-One of the things
you had to balance --

00:01:35.295 --> 00:01:36.329 line:92%
Sometimes it's just too late

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:39.599
when news breaks late on
Saturday to write a sketch,

00:01:39.599 --> 00:01:40.600 line:92%
obviously, but on "Update"

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.002 size:78% position:39%
you can get a joke in
every now and then.

00:01:43.002 --> 00:01:45.004 align:start size:94% position:6%
This Trump administration
I feel like

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
already famous
for late-breaking news.

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:50.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
Have you guys had to squeeze
stuff into "Update"?

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.711 line:92%
-Yeah, he keeps it exciting.

00:01:51.711 --> 00:01:54.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he's like -- It's like
being on "Chopped."

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:57.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
You ever watch that show
"Chopped"?

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:57.717 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:59.986
Where it's just, like,
a new ingredient for no reason?

00:01:59.986 --> 00:02:03.790
You're like, "All right. Now I
got to figure out how to --"

00:02:03.790 --> 00:02:05.058 line:92%
-How put sriracha on my pizza.

00:02:05.058 --> 00:02:09.529
-Sriracha for the dessert round?
Okay. I guess.

00:02:09.529 --> 00:02:13.600 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you guys --
the Hawaii disaster --

00:02:13.600 --> 00:02:17.403
I mean, not disaster, but of
the fake missile or false --

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a disaster among
husbands and wives

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:23.476 align:start size:94% position:6%
who thought it was happening
said something horrible,

00:02:23.476 --> 00:02:27.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they were, like,
"Take me back?"

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:28.615 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:29.682 line:92%
It happened like right before --

00:02:29.682 --> 00:02:31.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
-There was
a lot of apology notes.

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:34.621 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:38.525
-We were on -- It was then -- It
happened like a couple of hours

00:02:38.525 --> 00:02:39.192 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
before we were on,

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:42.428
and we were talking about doing
like a fake emergency alert

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:42.962 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on the show.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.898 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, missile
headed to New York.

00:02:44.898 --> 00:02:45.431 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.431 --> 00:02:46.199 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And then we were, like,

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:48.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, I think that
it's actually illegal,

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:49.702 size:75% position:38% line:92%
because we're on --"

00:02:49.702 --> 00:02:50.870 line:92%
We're live, and it's the news

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:52.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we were like,
"Maybe we shouldn't."

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.541 align:start size:94% position:6%
We realized
we had more restraint

00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:56.809 align:start size:94% position:6%
than the people
running the actual agency.

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:57.477 size:75% position:38% line:92%
Maybe this is crazy.

00:02:57.477 --> 00:03:00.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, somebody just, like,
pushed the button by accident.

00:03:00.647 --> 00:03:03.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, it should be way harder
to do that, right?

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:04.384 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:05.251 line:92%
Shouldn't you have to, like,

00:03:05.251 --> 00:03:08.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
two people turn a key
at the same time before you --

00:03:08.021 --> 00:03:10.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
-If you try to print something
in Microsoft Word,

00:03:10.623 --> 00:03:13.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's like, "Don't you want to
spell-check it?

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:16.462 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. "Did you mean?"
[ Laughter ]

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:19.199 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But now, I think that's
a mistake is we --

00:03:19.199 --> 00:03:21.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
now movies are ahead of
real life,

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.736
that every movie everything had
to be two keys,

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:28.241
and now we're like -- we are
literally a finger, everywhere.

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:30.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's like we don't watch
these movies

00:03:30.843 --> 00:03:32.078 line:92%
that tell us about the future.

00:03:32.078 --> 00:03:36.015
That's why -- it's like, I won't
buy a sex robot for that reason,

00:03:36.015 --> 00:03:39.786 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I know it's probably
going to try to kill me.

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:40.320 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:45.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's the why.
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:47.126 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Really thought it through.
-Yeah.

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.828 line:92%
-Really thought it through.

00:03:48.828 --> 00:03:51.931 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This isn't on TV is it?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:51.931 --> 00:03:53.733 line:92%
-Not all of it, obviously.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.635 line:92%
-We're gonna get one sent.

00:03:55.635 --> 00:03:56.469 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Another -- last week --

00:03:56.469 --> 00:04:01.541
-We get free stuff all the time
if we just mention a product.

00:04:01.541 --> 00:04:02.075 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.075 --> 00:04:05.745 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I've been trying to subtly
just mention products

00:04:05.745 --> 00:04:07.347 line:92%
to get it sent to me for free,

00:04:07.347 --> 00:04:11.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I'll let you know
if I get a sex robot or not.

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:11.985 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.985 --> 00:04:14.954
-I feel like --
-We've been doing the worst ones

00:04:14.954 --> 00:04:18.124 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I mentioned
the Kia Sorento the other day,

00:04:18.124 --> 00:04:19.592 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I'm like...
[ Laughter ]

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:21.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then he mentioned Gas-X
on the show,

00:04:21.828 --> 00:04:24.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they immediately sent him
a bunch of Gas-X.

00:04:24.797 --> 00:04:26.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, it's like --
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. I mentioned Lululemon
in this sketch

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:31.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
where I played
a liberal white woman.

00:04:31.638 --> 00:04:32.071 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:04:32.071 --> 00:04:34.007 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And they sent me
a bunch of Lululemon clothes,

00:04:34.007 --> 00:04:37.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now I got to explain that
to my family.

00:04:37.143 --> 00:04:37.677 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.677 --> 00:04:40.146
-I want to talk -- you played
Gretchen, a white liberal --

00:04:40.146 --> 00:04:44.183
and how much makeup were you in
to transform into a white woman?

00:04:44.183 --> 00:04:46.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I tried to go as method
as I could

00:04:46.452 --> 00:04:47.987 line:92%
with as much makeup as possible.

00:04:47.987 --> 00:04:49.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-Really unrecognizable.

00:04:49.956 --> 00:04:53.192
I won't tell the people watching
at home which one Che is,

00:04:53.192 --> 00:04:56.663
but he's one of those --
one of those three white women.

00:04:56.663 --> 00:04:59.065 align:start size:94% position:6%
When the Stormy Daniels story
happened,

00:04:59.065 --> 00:05:01.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
when that broke,
the crazy thing was,

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:03.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
the last time Donald Trump was
on the show,

00:05:03.836 --> 00:05:06.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
he was in a sketch
with Vanessa and Cecily,

00:05:06.673 --> 00:05:08.541 line:92%
who were playing porn stars.

00:05:08.541 --> 00:05:09.108 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's true.

00:05:09.108 --> 00:05:11.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you guys --
Did that occur to you

00:05:11.477 --> 00:05:13.346 line:92%
as quickly as it occurred to me?

00:05:13.346 --> 00:05:14.614 line:92%
-Yes. About instantaneously.

00:05:14.614 --> 00:05:17.383 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Because in the sketch,
at the end of it,

00:05:17.383 --> 00:05:18.017 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
he turns to Cecily,

00:05:18.017 --> 00:05:20.320
and he says, "Didn't you used to
be a brunette?"

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:24.524
And like, he's not going to ever
say that, and then he said it.

00:05:24.524 --> 00:05:25.058 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:25.058 --> 00:05:26.793 align:start size:94% position:6%
And literally right after it
says it,

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:29.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
it cuts to "Donald Trump
for President 2016."

00:05:29.862 --> 00:05:30.430 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It was insane.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.831 line:92%
-So you guys have a theory that

00:05:31.831 --> 00:05:33.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
people are actually
jealous of Trump,

00:05:33.766 --> 00:05:35.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
which not a lot of
people talk about.

00:05:35.435 --> 00:05:39.138
-I like that you said it as
though this is our known theory.

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:40.239 size:75% position:38% line:92%
We have this theory.

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:40.907 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-I wouldn't say jealous.

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:43.576
I just think they're waiting for
the other shoe to drop

00:05:43.576 --> 00:05:46.846 align:start size:94% position:6%
where he gets his comeuppance,
but it just seems to keep

00:05:46.846 --> 00:05:48.748 align:start size:94% position:6%
getting better and better
for him.

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:49.682 line:92%
And it's driving people nuts.

00:05:49.682 --> 00:05:52.518
Like, you know, the medical
report comes out about him,

00:05:52.518 --> 00:05:55.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, he's 239 and he can live
until he's 100 years old,

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:57.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're, like,
"How is that possible?!"

00:05:57.890 --> 00:05:58.424 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.424 --> 00:06:00.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
-People are basically
just really angry at him

00:06:00.827 --> 00:06:02.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he has great genes.
-Yeah.

00:06:02.395 --> 00:06:03.396 line:92%
-Like, he can just eat this --

00:06:03.396 --> 00:06:05.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
McDonald's five times a day
and he's fine.

00:06:05.231 --> 00:06:07.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And he does. His parents
lived to be very old.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.268 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, he's definitely
gonna be 90.

00:06:09.268 --> 00:06:10.169 align:start size:94% position:6%
-90 at the minimum.
-Yeah.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:12.939
Well, I have a theory that we're
gonna have tiny robots

00:06:12.939 --> 00:06:14.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
inside us
and we'll live until 250,

00:06:14.474 --> 00:06:16.609 align:start size:94% position:6%
but that's not what
this is about.

00:06:16.609 --> 00:06:17.143 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.143 --> 00:06:17.944 line:92%
We'll talk about that later.

00:06:17.944 --> 00:06:20.747
-Somebody's gonna get some
tiny robots sent to them.

00:06:20.747 --> 00:06:21.280 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.916 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sent inside them?

